## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Type definitions for CAPA (illustrative)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  status: 'proposed'|'in_progress'|'implemented'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure region-aware metrics and dashboards?
- What RCAs templates and safeguards would you require before closing a CAPA?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around data governance, cross-region containment, and traceability after a data-leak fault in a deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and evidence tagging
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle gates
- REST API design for CAPA management with linked logs/traces
- Regional leakage metrics and false positive handling
- RCA templates and canary rollback for data sinks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model in TypeScript
type CAPA = {
  capa_id: string;
  incident_time: string;
  data_class: string;
  evidence_refs: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owner: string;
  remediation: string;
  status: 'IDENTIFY'|'CONTAIN'|'INVESTIGATE'|'REMEDIATE'|'VERIFY'|'CLOSED';
  RCA_id?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with an existing audit log system?
- How would you enforce access controls for CAPA modification?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  redactionVersion: string;
  implicatedRegions: string[];
  tenantIds: string[];
  severity: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the effectiveness of the redaction rollback in production?
- Which metrics would you surface to product and compliance teams during a breach incident?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement data lineage capture across CDC and streaming layers?
- What rollback safety checks would you add to the canary plan?
